0e88edc03692dc1ff2aeacdcc37941665867","event_uuid":"4852d2c4-b220-452d-acc9-4d4ca17ea63f","position":{"commit_sha":"044abf4555d27bbce1c93a949a5abda8115cde2b","position":"1785768180782712001-4852d2c4-b220-452d-acc9-4d4ca17ea63f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d5b25c0ec702c3137ef091adf3744fb31e829f7f13e85be4ad64c98f5f500d58","event_uuid":"be6c357f-a4a2-4a6d-9ee8-66235c986eee","position":{"commit_sha":"044abf4555d27bbce1c93a949a5abda8115cde2b","position":"1785768181238739001-be6c357f-a4a2-4a6d-9ee8-66235c986eee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"First review returned INDETERMINATE because an Anthropic verifier call exhausted transport retries. Remediated the two surfaced no-verification findings before retry: the sidecar-only real-git AC now explicitly exercises both staging and basename membership, and the new module boundary is justified by the cohesive rotation seam plus current 749/799-line pressure on BindingStore/outbound_differ under the locked 800 cap.","timestamp":1785752366190430001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Signed PASS obtained after transport recovery. Advisory handling: execution will include both dual-write and sidecar-only real-git cases, so child AC3 does not mask the parent basename requirement; preflight will run the repository module-size gate plus direct line counts for binding_store.py, outbound_differ.py, and get_rotation.py, enforcing <=800 and the no-tiny-extraction policy. Remaining compound wording is retained where bytes plus HEAD are two facets of one atomic no-write contract.","timestamp":1785768175770125001}],"created_at":1785372488628349001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e3a728ea-eef4-485f-933c-a05612ed05ce","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"f7ee-572b-1eb0-4af8"}],"description":"Move GET-rotation stamps into `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json` so a later rollout step can remove them from the large sort-ordered `bindings.json`. A2-1 is the compatibility half: new binaries write both formats and read `max(new, legacy)`; A2-2 removes the legacy write after its observable rollout gate. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** contains the measured facts.\n\n## Why\n\n`set_last_get` stamps `last_get_pass` on up to `deletion_probe_limit` (default 20) bound-but-absent keys per pass. Measured: exactly 20 entries change per affected pass. The full A2 saving is realized only after A2-2 removes this scattered legacy write. During A2-1, dual-write is intentional compatibility cost: an old binary cannot read the sidecar, so it must still observe progress made by new binaries.\n\n## Approach — compatibility first\n\nWrite every new stamp to the sidecar and the legacy inline field, and read the chronological `max(sidecar, legacy)`. Under mixed versions an old binary may advance only the inline field; `max()` ensures a following new binary does not use stale sidecar state. Conversely, dual-write ensures an old binary following a new one sees the new progress. Values are fixed-width zero-padded timestamps, so lexicographic `max()` is chronological.\n\nLoad legacy-only rotation state in memory and persist the sidecar only through `BindingStore.save()`. This covers all production save paths: end-of-pass persistence, the write-ahead saves in `dispatch_one.py`, and the recovery/retirement saves in `binding_store.py`. Saving unchanged canonical state must remain byte-stable. `reconcile-check` runs with `persist=False`, never reaches save, and must not create the sidecar.\n\nThe new `get_rotation.py` boundary is deliberate rather than a generic sidecar abstraction. At the reviewed base, `binding_store.py` is 749 lines and `outbound_differ.py` is 799 lines; putting the cohesive load/canonicalize/effective-max/dual-write/atomic-save cluster into either near-cap module would violate or threaten the locked 800-line policy. The cluster is an existing call-graph seam: `BindingStore` delegates sidecar state operations and invokes its save operation from `BindingStore.save()`, while `outbound_differ` continues coding against duck-typed accessors and imports no concrete BindingStore. This keeps the established BindingStore persistence lifecycle without duplicating sibling-sidecar scaffolding inside it. The extracted module must satisfy the repository minimum-file and target-size policy.\n\nAdd `git_adapter.GET_ROTATION_FILE`, characterize its path, and include it in both `reconcile_helpers.py` explicit staging and basename membership checks. This is required because local reconciliation does not use `git add -A`. A sidecar-only real-git case must prove the basename check is load-bearing rather than being masked by a simultaneously changed `bindings.json`. The existing `.gitattributes` glob covers the new file. Update the `_store/push.py` docstring that enumerates regenerable files.\n\n## Rollback\n\nReverting A2-1 is safe: a reverted reader ignores the sidecar but every new-binary pass also advanced the inline legacy field. The orphaned sidecar is inert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] After rotation state is initialized, an idempotent real-repo pass with no absent-key GETs leaves all committed bridge-state files byte-identical and does not advance HEAD. Tier: integration in a real temporary git repository.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A pass with at most 20 absent-key GETs advances identical selected-key stamps in `get_rotation.json` and the legacy inline fields. Tier: integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] With only `get_rotation.json` changed, the explicit local commit path stages and commits the sidecar without `git add -A`; this exercises both the staging list and basename membership check. Tier: real-git integration.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Rotation order after an interleaved old-binary/new-binary pass sequence matches the all-new sequence. Tier: integration; it must fail for either sidecar-first lookup or missing dual-write.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A legacy inline-only store yields identical rotation order. Tier: unit.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A legacy inline-only store materializes equivalent sidecar state on its next persisted save. Tier: unit.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store leaves `git status --porcelain` empty. Tier: CLI subprocess.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store does not create `get_rotation.json`. Tier: CLI subprocess.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `git_adapter.GET_ROTATION_FILE` names `.bridge_state/get_rotation.json`. Tier: git-adapter characterization.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The `_store/push.py` regenerable-files documentation includes `get_rotation.json`. Tier: characterization test.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `outbound_differ.py` remains at or below 800 lines. Verify with the repository module-size gate.\n\n## Files\n\n`binding_store.py`, new `get_rotation.py`, `outbound_differ.py`, `git_adapter.py`, `reconcile_helpers.py`, `_store/push.py` (docstring), focused tests.\n\nScope: M. Depends on closed A1.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Rotation dual-read, dual-write, and sidecar persistence"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/get_rotation.py","reason":"Own get_rotation.json compatibility and persistence helpers"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"Move fail-open rotation helpers out under the 800-line cap"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/git_adapter.py","reason":"Define the canonical get_rotation.json relative path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"Stage get_rotation.json explicitly"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push.py","reason":"Document the regenerable sidecar"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"Unit, integration, real-git, CLI read-only, and characterization coverage"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","f7ee-572b-1eb0-4af8"],["parent","0303-692c-55dc-4a18"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","parent_status_uuid":"4852d2c4-b220-452d-acc9-4d4ca17ea63f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9594-1f1c-bcd1-4774","ticket_type":"story","title":"A2-1: move last_get_pass rotation bookkeeping into .bridge_state/get_rotation.json (write-new, read max(new, legacy))","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0310427b-6072-4bb4-ad8e-3033ed4aaa2f","e3a728ea-eef4-485f-933c-a05612ed05ce","12fca844-90f2-45c5-bbd8-4da68ed3b315","b0698e3c-2e1b-4da3-8910-e5eb207d9887","3fdcd974-62cb-4c97-a14e-dd449ea4c885","2f8b9b80-6f79-4e03-9a0f-429272102cd8","4250a5f1-162d-4b55-89bb-d6653858821b","b6c9cffa-7b3b-4a68-84c1-8bc673ba24a5","b55afd99-a48c-4793-9658-184a12e3808b","9ddd1b2f-f114-4b00-8ae6-a710a85bdfae","4852d2c4-b220-452d-acc9-4d4ca17ea63f","be6c357f-a4a2-4a6d-9ee8-66235c986eee"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785768181238739002,"uuid":"7b7fec80-ea04-498e-86c9-